  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, VRChat allows users to display original system models for FBT trackers via the \"FBT Tracker Model -> System\" setting. It would be highly beneficial to introduce the exact same toggle for primary VR controllers, allowing them to remain permanently visible in-game.\n\nImplementing this would provide three main benefits:\n\nDesign Consistency: It unifies the tracking visualization system. Controllers and trackers should share the same display options for a more cohesive user experience.\n\nCustomization: SteamVR allows users to replace controller models in its local files. Rendering these system models natively in VRChat would let players see their personalized controller skins globally.\n\nDebugging: Just like with FBT trackers, being able to see the exact real-world position and rotation of the controllers in-game can be a valuable tool for troubleshooting tracking issues and IK calibration.",
